  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "UNIQUE deduplicates text case-insensitively keeping the first spelling, while comparing numbers by binary64 value",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527.20088, UNIQUE compares text case-insensitively and retains the first spelling encountered (CONCAT(UNIQUE({\"a\";\"A\";\"b\"})) returns \"ab\"), whereas numbers are compared by exact binary64 value without a tolerance window, so 0.3 and 0.1+0.2 remain distinct (ROWS(UNIQUE(VSTACK(0.3,0.1+0.2))) returns 2).",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in Excel 16.0.20527.20088 in f3_arrays (rows 15-18) and matched across 1,277 of 1,277 full-bank UNIQUE rows (dc-ymjf.2.10).",
